    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n35022" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἔναρχος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>,
			(<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀρχή</span>) <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>in office, in authority</i>, <i><span class="en">
				App.
				<u>BC</u>
				1.14
			</span></i>, Wilcken <i><span class="en">
				<u>Chr.</u>
				41 iii 10
			</span></i>
			<span class="entity">(iii A. D.)</span>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οἱ ἔ. ὄντες ἀεί</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>GDI</u>
					2520.12
				</span></i>
			 (Delph.); <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">συνέδρους ἀεὶ τοὺς
			ἐ</span>. those <i>who were in office</i> at the time, <i><span class="en">
